      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "ALWAYSBDREAMING (2) was a beaten favourite here last time but she was brave as she had to race three wide without cover but fought on well to go under narrowly. That was her fourth placing from five starts so her hoof is on the till. With better luck she can break through. AMERICAN SUCCESS (1) is a three-year-old colt by American Ideal on debut. The inside draw is a big aid to a debutant and he showed ability in winning a Victorian trial so could make an immediate impact. VELOX FIRE (10) is another at the track for the first time. By leading sire Always B Miki and hails from the James Rattray stable. Has strong trial form coming into this, winning his latest hitout at Menangle. Draws on the back row but could measure right up. Last-start placegetter GOOD TALK (6) is worth including again.",
